  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-22: promote_to_branch corrected from feature/pAI-s17-hermes-chat-identity to feature/pAI-s16-offline-reconciliation. arch-ctm caught scope-boundary conflict: AI.17 (docs/plans/phase-ai/sprint-ai-17-hermes-chat-identity.md) is scoped strictly to the ambient chat-context resolver and states 'may run in parallel with AI.11-AI.16 because it does not modify atm-graft, daemon transport, HTTP, storage, or a shared Phase AI contract' -- dispatching an unrelated crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs visibility fix there would break that parallel-safety contract. This finding is a workspace-wide repeatable pattern present on all branches s11-s17 and is not uniquely owned by AI.16 either, but s16 carries no equivalent narrow-scope restriction, so it is bundled onto the same corrected fix-assignment batch for dispatch efficiency rather than left on the out-of-scope s17 branch. Original mis-target was applied via unverified highest-open-branch heuristic." .

